  "problem": "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that $\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\{{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3},{v}_{1}-{v}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent\n\nII. $\\{{v}_{1},2{v}_{2},3{v}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent\n\nIII. $\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},0\\}$ is linearly independent",
